IMPORTANT — WORKING DRAFT, NOT A LICENSE GRANT
This document records the maintainer's intended terms for review. It is
not the final, effective license and grants no rights on its own.
A final version must be reviewed for legal enforceability, third-party
rights and compatibility, approved by the rights holder, and published
before any public software release. Do not distribute this draft as if
it were a legally validated open-source license.

1. Scope
"Software" means CS2 Companion Studio source and executable code
released under these terms, including modified versions and derivative
works incorporating copyrightable portions of that code. Separately
licensed third-party components remain subject to their own terms.

2. Permitted use and private modifications (in the eventual final license)
The intended permission is worldwide, nonexclusive and royalty-free.
Anyone may study, run, reproduce and modify the Software, including
for personal, educational, nonprofit or professional/business purposes.
Private and purely internal modifications need not be published.

Use during monetized streaming, sponsored content, professional esports
training, paid coaching and similar activities is permitted; such use
does not, by itself, count as selling a copy of the Software.

3. Free sharing and code transparency
Anyone may redistribute the unmodified Software or a modified version
without charging for access, in source or executable form, provided
they:
- preserve the copyright notice and these license conditions;
- clearly identify material modifications;
- give recipients free access to the corresponding source code for
  executable versions they redistribute; and
- retain the same no-resale and source-disclosure obligations for
  covered modified versions.

No duty to share source arises solely from private/internal use.

4. Prohibition on selling the Software
Recipients may not charge, require payment or impose a paid subscription
as a condition of obtaining a copy or license of the Software, including
a modified version. This applies to source downloads, executables,
installers, paid "Pro" editions and bundles in which payment is required
to obtain the covered Software.

Recipients must not provide paid-only access to the functionality of a
hosted modified version of the Software as a substitute for selling it.

An entirely voluntary donation is allowed only when the same Software
and all its covered functionality remain genuinely available for free,
without a paywall or exclusive software benefits.

Permission to sell copies or licenses may be granted separately only
by the rights holder in writing.

5. Paid work distinguished from sale of the Software
Professional use does not become prohibited merely because a person
earns income from an activity using the Software. Charging for coaching,
training or separately commissioned programming work (including bug
fixes, custom widgets and new features) is intended to be permitted.
Such a payment must not be a disguised mandatory charge for obtaining
or licensing the Software or a covered modified copy.

If commissioned modifications are later distributed, the obligations
in section 3 apply to those distributions.

6. Hosted modified versions
A person who makes a modified version available for interactive use
over a network must offer users of that version the corresponding
modified source code without charge, even when no executable copy is
distributed. Solely private use does not create a public-disclosure
obligation.

7. Attribution, names and third-party rights
The copyright notice and license conditions must accompany copies.
Forks must not misrepresent themselves as the official CS2 Companion
Studio project or claim endorsement from Shibxtshi, Valve, FACEIT,
OpenAI or other unaffiliated organizations. No trademark rights are
granted. All third-party assets and dependencies keep their own rights
and licenses.

8. Disclaimer
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED
BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE RIGHTS HOLDER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR DAMAGES
ARISING FROM USE OF THE SOFTWARE.

9. Open drafting questions — MUST BE RESOLVED BEFORE PUBLICATION
- Draw a clear and enforceable line between separately billed setup,
  hosting, maintenance and support services and a disguised software
  paywall; some of these scenarios remain disputed.
- Determine which obligations can legitimately apply to independent
  tutorials, themes and third-party creations that copy no Software.
- Review derivative-work boundaries, paid bundles, brand/fork naming,
  network source disclosure and compatibility with third-party licenses.
- Obtain a qualified intellectual-property legal review and approve
  an operative final license.

This is a CUSTOM SOURCE-AVAILABLE DRAFT, not an Open Source Initiative
approved open-source license. The copyright holder's choice of a
no-resale term means it cannot truthfully be marketed as OSI-open-source.
